<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilhelm Karl, Duke of Urach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1864">1864</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Mindaugas II, Wilhelm of Urach, Prince Wilhelm of Urach</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilhelm Karl, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-urach">Urach</a>, was a German prince and general of a Catholic branch of the royal house of Württemberg. On 11 July 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-lithuania">Council of Lithuania</a> elected him king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindaugas">Mindaugas</a> II, hoping a monarchy would loosen German control. He never went to Lithuania, and the council revoked the election in November 1918 as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> collapsed.</p></div>
